WEBVTT

00:11:28.552 --> 00:11:30.933
in offices, in classrooms,

00:11:30.957 --> 00:11:32.504
in the eyes of the government,

00:11:32.528 --> 00:11:34.266
in romantic situations,

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:36.123
and for some of us,

00:11:36.147 --> 00:11:38.880
even in the mirror
when we wake up in the morning.

00:11:39.973 --> 00:11:44.044
But our gender mistakes
have the potential for something good.

00:11:44.687 --> 00:11:45.950
Even in the binary,

00:11:45.974 --> 00:11:48.371
approaching life on the stage
as a man or a woman,

00:11:48.395 --> 00:11:51.371
we can support each other
in experimentation,

00:11:51.395 --> 00:11:52.655
trips and stumbles,

00:11:52.679 --> 00:11:54.672
two-hour-long meditations on

00:11:54.696 --> 00:11:57.006
or five-second costume
changes with gender.

00:11:57.030 --> 00:11:59.045
And failure is a key part

00:11:59.069 --> 00:12:01.522
of Judith Butler's theory
of performativity.